  "description": "A rejected result is permanent for its opId: resending it is a duplicate even after the cause is gone, and a retry needs a new opId. Also: create on a trashed id is RECORD_EXISTS, restore on a live record is RECORD_NOT_DELETED, unset removes a field, and tombstone, restore, set and create on recordKind document are OP_UNSUPPORTED. Values must be valid archive records: a create whose bookId does not exist, or whose parentId is not an existing manuscriptNode, is REFERENCE_UNRESOLVED; a create with a wrongly typed required field (title as a number) is INVALID_VALUE. Both are rejected with nothing applied and nothing stored, so the pull after them is empty.",
